coverage/

# Logs
snowflake.log
npm-debug.log*

# package-lock.json is intentionally not committed.
#
# As a published npm library we don't ship our lock file to customers, so they
# resolve our dependency ranges fresh (new projects, no lockfile). Committing a
# lock file here would let CI/dev builds pass against pinned transitive versions
# that our users never get, hiding breakage until they report it.
#
# Running installs unlocked gives us an early signal when a downstream
# dependency release breaks resolution. Example: in May 2026 an aws-sdk minor
# silently dropped Node 18 support and we caught it in CI before customers did.
#
# Trade-off: this makes main more susceptible to breakage from an upstream
# release landing between merges. The preferred fix is to bump/adjust our
# declared ranges when a release breaks us; pinning an exact version is also
# acceptable when there's no alternative.
package-lock.json
